# Animation clips.  Two directories, and the split is what keeps a 160 MB file
# out of a commit: notebook 27 writes its RAW renders to img/raw/ (about 225 MB
# for the seven scenes, an hour of compute), and only the shrunk publishable
# copies -- around 15 MB for the set, after tools/make_demo_video.py -- live in
# img/ and are tracked, the same treatment img/gallery/*.png gets.
#
# If both had shared a path, the next RENDER = True would quietly replace the
# committed clips with the raw ones, and the size would only be noticed at
# `git push`.  None of this reaches PyPI: [tool.setuptools.packages.find] looks
# only under src/, so the sdist and the wheel never see img/ at all.
img/raw/
img/*.mp4
img/.palette.png
